faqs:
  - q: "Do Google Ads work for dentists?"
    a: "They can. People search Google when they need a dentist, and \"dentist near me\" alone gets about 1.8 million searches a month in the US. Ads put your practice in front of the people searching in your area. How well they work depends on your budget, how many other dentists nearby are advertising and the page the ad sends people to."
  - q: "What is dental PPC?"
    a: "PPC stands for pay-per-click. It's another name for ads like Google Ads, where you only pay when someone clicks your ad. Dental PPC just means pay-per-click ads for a dental practice."
  - q: "How much should I spend on Google Ads?"
    a: "It depends on your area, how many other dentists nearby are advertising and how many new patients you want. I'll help you pick an amount that fits your goals, and you can change it later. Your ad budget is paid directly to Google, separate from my fee."
  - q: "How soon will I get calls?"
    a: "Your ads can start showing once Google has verified your account and approved the ads. How quickly calls come in depends on your area and your budget."
  - q: "Do I need a new website?"
    a: "Not always. Ads work best when they send people to a page about the exact thing they searched for, so building that page is part of the setup. If your whole site needs work, I build <a href=\"/services#s-website\">websites</a> too."
  - q: "Do you also do SEO?"
    a: "Yes. SEO takes a few months to work, but over time it costs a lot less than ads. I'll tell you which one I'd start with for your practice. You can see both on my <a href=\"/services#q-market\">services page</a>."
  - q: "How is working with you different from a dental PPC agency?"
    a: "An agency usually gives you an account manager with a team behind them. With me, the person you talk to is the person who sets up your ads, builds the page they lead to and checks the results every month."
  - q: "Do you work with practices outside California?"
    a: "Yes. I'm based in Monterey, California, and I work with businesses all over the US over Zoom."
---
